  "title": "# Build: build-todo-sync (FABLE, high thinking: builds-store schema + cross-app sync contract = fou…",
  "asked": "# Build: build-todo-sync (FABLE, high thinking: builds-store schema + cross-app sync contract = foundation) ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voice) \"For every build from now on, like this plugin build, prompt me for a name which will be used to reference it in the to-do manager. Then we're going to add a list in the to-do manager with all the steps that Orchestrator broke it into. And then it will check off each one in real time as the orchestrator processes each step. So the to-do list for every build has the same exact steps as items in the to-do list that the orchestrator broke the build down into. The builds into categories: plugins, plugin extensions, add-ons, framework, app, feature, module. Sync the build manager with the to-do manager and the real-time checklist. Put this in the planner.\" Then: \"Immediately, number two behind the eavesdropper.\" The Plan Studio plan 'Build names + live to-do checklists' holds the same spec. Link this build to it and mark the plan building. Book to a free named agent. ## Do 1. **Build name**: a required `displayName` on every build (builds store schema + migration). Every way a build is created (console Build manager, orchestrator, build_start MCP/CLI, voice through Amber, packager, handoff) **prompts Brett for a short name** (suggests one, editable). The name shows everywhere (Build manager, to-do manager, chat, ledger, crew cards). 2. **Category**: a required `category` enum on every build: **Plugin, Plugin extension, Add-on, Framework, App, Feature, Module**. Suggested automatically from what it touches, Brett confirms. Filters and grouping by category in every build list. Backfill existing builds (best guess, flagged for review). 3. **To-do list per build in the AmberX to-do manager** (amberx lists/items): a list named after the build, nested under a category parent list ('Builds › Plugin › <name>'). Its items are **exactly the orchestrator's steps, in order**, each with model/thinking/agent in the item details and a link back to the build/step. 4. **Live check-off**: when a step finishes, its to-do item checks off instantly (event push; no polling). Mirror everything: step added/removed/re-split, reorder, handed to a helper (assignee shown), held/rejected/blocked (status icons), build done (list marked complete) or cancelled (list archived). 5. **Sync contract** (`build-todo-sync@1`): the builds store is the source of truth. The to-do list is a synced view. Ticking or unticking an item in the to-do manager is owner-only and confirms before changing the step. Idempotent, with conflict-safe reconciliation and a Systems-check row + Auto fix if they drift. 6. Backfill all open builds into lists. Completed builds from the last 7 days go in as completed lists. 7. Basic Markdown readme (standing rule). Tests, UI Review shots (non-blocking), PR, auto-land, redeploy the console and AmberX web. Report in _claude/builds/reports/. Commits clean. ## ADDENDUM 1 (Brett, voice, Nov 4) \"This is a plugin too.\" - Package it as a **plugin** (`plugin@1`, e.g. 'Build to-do sync', `forFramework: true` so its commands get Molly voice commands automatically): name prompt UI, category picker, list creation, live check-off, two-way sync, Systems-check row, settings (settings-interface@1), and its API/MCP/CLI commands, all inside the plugin. It can be enabled/disabled and installed via Plugin Manager. - Only the builds-store fields (`displayName`, `category` + migration) and the `build-todo-sync@1` contract live in the framework (Fable). Everything else is plugin code. - When disabled, builds still work, and the to-do lists just stop syncing (with a visible note). Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voic…",
